## 11. Automatic Sign-Out After Inactivity

Implement or improve automatic sign-out after a configurable period of user inactivity.

First inspect the existing authentication provider and session-management implementation.

Requirements:

1. Track meaningful user activity using an appropriate mechanism.
2. Reset the inactivity period when the user interacts with the application.
3. Sign the user out after the configured inactivity period.
4. Display a warning before automatic sign-out, where practical.
5. Provide a clear way for the user to continue their session if it is still valid.
6. Clear protected client-side state after sign-out.
7. Redirect the user to the appropriate login page.
8. Ensure protected pages cannot be accessed after the session has expired or become invalid.
9. Avoid unnecessary timers or duplicate event listeners.
10. Clean up timers and event listeners when they are no longer needed.

Use a reasonable default of **30 minutes of inactivity**, unless the existing system has an established timeout policy that must be preserved.

Make the timeout configurable where appropriate.

Do not confuse inactivity sign-out with the backend authentication token's expiration. Respect the authentication provider's actual session state and token validity.

Do not claim that the server session has been invalidated unless the appropriate sign-out operation actually performs that action.

