**Prioritize functional correctness, data consistency, security, and maintainability over superficial visual changes.**

Do not merely describe the changes or provide a proposed design. Implement the requested improvements in the existing project wherever the available tools and environment permit.

Do not rewrite the entire application unless the current architecture demonstrably prevents a safe implementation.

Do not fabricate data, successful test results, completed integrations, or database operations.

Preserve existing user data, established relationships, role-based access controls, and unrelated working functionality.

If a requirement is already implemented correctly, retain it and verify it rather than duplicating it.

If a requirement is only partially implemented, improve the existing implementation.

If a requirement depends on a missing schema field, external service, or unavailable configuration, identify the dependency and make the safest compatible change possible.

**The final result must be a cohesive, functional AgriCycle application—not just a redesigned interface—with the requested improvements integrated into the existing system.**